	(text "LM5013 5.0V Out Buck Converter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.748 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 7.62 7.62)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3c40ea8a-5102-45a1-a40d-fda86f400c28")
	)
	(text "Notes\n\n1.	36V - 75V input, 5V output. 1A out max\n2.	Switching frequency of 300kHz\n3.	Inductor selection\n	-	Max peak-to-peak ripple current: 0.4A\n	-	Min inductance: 37.3uH\n	-	Selected inductor: SRN8040TA-470M (BOURNS)\n		>	2.2A saturation, 2A RMS current\n		>	Peak inductor current: 1.16A \n4.	Freewheel diode selected: V8P12-M3/86A (VISHAY)\n	-	V_{F}: 0.59V\n	-	R_{θJA}: 60°C/W\n	-	Min duty cycle: 0.065\n	-	Average diode current: 1 x (1-0.065) = 0.935A\n	-	Temperature rise: 33°C\n5.	Output capacitor selection\n	-	Allowable voltage ripple: 0.5%\n	-	Min capacitance: 5.29uF\n	-	To acccount for derating, 2 25V rated 22uF capacitors are chosen\n6.	Input capacitor selection\n	-	High-frequency input capacitance of 4.4uF or higher is reccomended. We choose 4 x 10uF cacitors. These capacitors are derated to 1.5uF at 75V for a total of 6uF\n7.	PGOOD is high impedance when FB voltage exceeds 95% of V_{REF}, allowing the line to be pulled high. It is pulled to GND otherwise"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.272 41.656 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "58d11e3b-9f14-4d40-8b0e-5386afb38dd0")
	)
